@startuml
title ExplicitEuler fixed-grid lifecycle

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor Caller

package dynamics {
  interface DynamicalSystem {
    +state_dimension
    +vector_field(t, state)
  }
}

package simulation {
  interface NumericalMethod {
    +integrate(problem, request)
  }

  class InitialValueProblem
  class SimulationRequest {
    +t_span
    +max_step
    +output_times
  }
  class SimulationRunner
  class ExplicitEuler {
    +progress
    +step_observer
    +integrate(problem, request)
  }
  component "integrate_fixed_grid(...)" as FixedGrid
  component "advance(...)" as Advance
  component "apply_step(candidate)" as ApplyStep
  class IntegrationStep
  class IntegrationData
  class Solution
}

ExplicitEuler ..|> NumericalMethod
InitialValueProblem --> ExplicitEuler : dynamics and initial state
SimulationRequest --> ExplicitEuler : temporal request
DynamicalSystem --> InitialValueProblem : physical capability

Caller --> SimulationRunner : simulate(problem, method, request)
SimulationRunner --> NumericalMethod : integrate(...)
ExplicitEuler --> FixedGrid : initial state, request, advance
SimulationRequest --> FixedGrid : main grid and saved times
FixedGrid --> Advance : main or shadow callback
Advance --> ApplyStep : fixed t and duration
ApplyStep --> DynamicalSystem : vector_field(t, state)
Advance ..> IntegrationStep : main step when observer exists
ExplicitEuler --> IntegrationData : times, states, step_count
IntegrationData --> SimulationRunner : validated physical output
SimulationRunner --> Solution : immutable result

note right of FixedGrid
  Main call: observe = true
  Shadow call: observe = false

  A shadow starts from the preceding
  main node and never changes the
  accepted main trajectory.
end note

note right of ApplyStep
  state_next = state + h f(t, state)
  One validated field evaluation
  per invocation
end note

note bottom of IntegrationStep
  Copies both snapshots and exposes
  the same captured apply_step map.
end note

@enduml

